From 89c66f6fecfae5e18cc38bb3c4ea575e436bf1b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JSwetz <Johnswetz1982@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 03:26:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(build): pin test fixtures and post goldens to LF line
 endings

Git for Windows checks out text files with CRLF by default.
Pin golden files, machine files, model fixtures, skills, and workflows to LF in .gitattributes.
Normalize line endings for fig8.step.
Add tests in xtask to assert the LF line ending attribute and verify checkout with core.autocrlf=true.

Fixes #2840
---
 .gitattributes                                |   21 +-
 .../2840-gitattributes-crlf-fixtures.md       |    9 +
 testdata/models/fig8.step                     | 1952 ++++++++---------
 xtask/tests/example_line_endings.rs           |   96 +
 4 files changed, 1101 insertions(+), 977 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 docs/decisions/2840-gitattributes-crlf-fixtures.md

diff --git a/.gitattributes b/.gitattributes
index f02afb959..0c4da7366 100644
--- a/.gitattributes
+++ b/.gitattributes
@@ -1,6 +1,25 @@
 # Golden outputs are compared byte for byte (the post writes LF line
 # ends): pin them to LF in every checkout, whatever core.autocrlf says.
-crates/app/tests/golden/** text eol=lf
+crates/*/tests/golden/** text eol=lf
+crates/*/tests/recorded/** text eol=lf
+crates/*/tests/fixtures/** text eol=lf
+
+# Machine definitions and fixture descriptions are included or parsed with LF.
+crates/*/tests/**/*.mch text eol=lf
+assets/machines/**/*.mch text eol=lf
+
+# 3D models and test fixtures are parsed with LF line ends.
+testdata/**/*.step text eol=lf
+testdata/**/*.stp text eol=lf
+testdata/**/*.stl text eol=lf
+testdata/**/*.obj text eol=lf
+
+# Skill and agent definitions are parsed by xtask tests with LF.
+.claude/** text eol=lf
+
+# GitHub workflows and scripts run on Linux and are parsed with LF line ends.
+.github/** text eol=lf
+
 # Tester-kit programs are pinned byte for byte by their tests, like the goldens.
 docs/tester-kits/**/*.nc text eol=lf
 # Shipped example programs, including the catalog, are pinned byte for byte.
diff --git a/docs/decisions/2840-gitattributes-crlf-fixtures.md b/docs/decisions/2840-gitattributes-crlf-fixtures.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..b031202bd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/decisions/2840-gitattributes-crlf-fixtures.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+## #2840 - pin golden, machine, STEP and workflow fixtures to LF in .gitattributes
+
+- **Chosen:** pin all test fixtures, golden post outputs, machine definitions, STEP/STP models, agent and skill definitions, and GitHub workflows to LF line endings (`text eol=lf`) in `.gitattributes`.
+  - Why: Git for Windows checks out text files with CRLF by default (`core.autocrlf=true`). Test suites comparing post programs byte-for-byte (such as `explain_fanuc_family`), parsing machine definitions (such as `wire-iso-fixture.mch`), importing STEP models (`import_step_curve_guard`), and xtask tests parsing skill markdown or workflow concurrency blocks expect and require LF line endings (`\n`).
+  - Dropped: modifying individual tests to accept CRLF. Normalizing line endings at the repository boundary via `.gitattributes` guarantees deterministic behavior across platforms without weakening byte-exact golden test assertions.
+- **Pinning tests:**
+  - `xtask/tests/example_line_endings.rs`: added `all_golden_and_fixture_files_have_eol_lf` asserting that `git check-attr eol` reports `lf` across all golden, recorded, machine, STEP, skill, and workflow directories.
+  - `xtask/tests/example_line_endings.rs`: added `golden_and_fixture_files_keep_lf_with_autocrlf` asserting that checked-out files maintain LF line endings without carriage returns under `core.autocrlf=true`.
+  - Verified affected suites pass cleanly: `explain_fanuc_family`, `wire_taper_angle`, `import_step_curve_guard`, and `post_merge_concurrency`.
